tent="1-143723">Learn more about Southwark Green Investment</div><div data-ai-no-open-words="" data-content="1-143724">The fourth phase of Southwark Green Investment closed in March 2026, taking the total raised to £3.5 million. The next phase of investment will be launching soon, sign up for updates to get more news.</div><div data-ai-no-open-button-text="" data-content="1-143725">Sign up for updates</div><div data-ai-no-open-button-url="" data-content="1-143726">/signup-for-updates</div><div data-ai-no-past-invest-header="" data-content="1-143727">Placeholder</div><div data-ai-no-past-invest-copy="" data-content="1-143728">placeholder</div><div data-ai-no-past-invest-button-url="" data-content="1-143729">/</div><div data-ai-no-past-invest-button-text="" data-content="1-143730">Learn more</div><div data-ai-no-chart-img-url="" data-content="1-143731">https://cdn4.sharein.com/abundance/cms/fd81e4f6-d21a-4e91-84fd-4b7e41b130f2.jpg</div><div data-ai-no-chart-img-alt="" data-content="1-143732">An image of a greening project</div><div data-ai-no-chart-img-caption="" data-content="2-143733">The council has been investing in greening projects across the borough</div></div><section class="position-relative bg-colour--primary-surface p-t-spacer-4xl type-white ai-hero" style="background:#00873b"><div class="container"><div class="row brand-media-box align-items-start"><div class="col-12 col-md-8"><h1 class="text-choke-md--640 text-center--md font-secondary" style="color:#fff" data-content="1-143734">Southwark Council</h1><p class="body--xl text-choke-md--640 text-center--md m-b-spacer-sm" style="color:#fff" data-content="2-143738"><span>Help Southwark take local climate action to make its environment clean, green and healthy.</span></p></div><div class="col-12 col-md-4"><div class="ai-heroLogoRail"><img class="image-responsive hero-header__illustration brand-media-box__img" src="https://cdn4.sharein.com/abundance/cms/463c6908-a912-4085-a05a-47d779521797.png" alt="Southwark Council logo" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high"></div></div></div></div></section><div class="bg-colour--primary-surface bg-mask bg-mask--b-convex m-b-spacer-2xl ai-hero-mask" style="background:#00873b"></div><div id="ai-scope-wrap"><section class="m-b-spacer-lg ai-scope"><div class="container text-choke-960"><div class="row"><div class="col-12 text-center" data-content="2-143743"><p class="body--xl">Southwark Council is leading the way with climate action that makes its air cleaner, its borough greener and lives healthier. It has an ambitious strategy and action plan to transform Southwark into a carbon neutral borough by 2030. Its vision aims to reshape the borough into a better place for everyone, delivering improvements in health, raising the standard of homes, creating good green jobs and strengthening its communities.</p><p class="body--xl">The council has cut emissions by 23% since 2018 by working with communities to improve homes, streets and green spaces. This includes a number of climate projects, from an innovative heat pump programme for council housing estates, through to replacing all 17,000 streetlight light bulbs with LEDs. Now it wants to accelerate its work, and Southwark Green Investment is a chance for everyone to get involved. The council wants to raise £6m by 2030 through a series of investments, to fund a range of projects from its climate programme..</p><p class="body--xl text-center"></p><blockquote class="brand-blockquote"><p class="font-secondary">We're taking urgent action in Southwark to tackle the climate emergency – but we know the scale of the challenge means we can't do it alone. Southwark Green Investment is your chance to join us as we transform the borough.<br><br> Every investment, from as little as £5, will not only play its part in helping us hit our ambitious net-zero emissions target, but it will also help us to create a greener, fairer and safer borough.</p><footer class="choke-600 w-100 mx-auto"><img loading="lazy" src="https://cdn4.sharein.com/abundance/faa5cbba-a388-45f9-8f20-92240f1a10fe.png" alt="Rowan Ree" title="Image: https://cdn4.sharein.com/abundance/721452c5-0310-4766-847e-fbca0e347335.png"><div><p>Cllr John Batteson</p><cite>Cabinet Member for Climate Emergency, Jobs &amp; Business</cite></div></footer></blockquote></div></div></div></section><div class="bg-colour--primary-surface bg-mask bg-mask--t-convex ai-no-open-mask ai-scope" style="background-color: rgb(255, 237, 204);"></div><section class="home-green-investing position-relative p-y-spacer-xs bg-colour--primary-surface ai-no-open ai-scope" style="background-color: rgb(255, 237, 204);"><div class="container"><div class="row"><div class="col-12"><div class="flex-center"><h2 class="text-center m-b-spacer-sm">Learn more about Southwark Green Investment</h2></div><div class="flex-center"><p class="body--lg text-center choke-800 m-b-spacer-sm">The fourth phase of Southwark Green Investment closed in March 2026, taking the total raised to £3.5 million. The next phase of investment will be launching soon, sign up for updates to get more news.</p></div><div class="flex-center ai-no-open-btn-wrap"><a href="/signup-for-updates" class="brand-btn-grey--bordered brand-btn-grey--bordered--bordered btn btn--lg m-y-spacer-md btn--icon" style="border-color:#4c4c4a;color:#4c4c4a">Sign up for updates</a></div></div></div></div></section><div class="bg-colour--primary-surface bg-mask bg-mask--b-convex ai-no-open-mask ai-scope" style="background-color: rgb(255, 237, 204);"></div><div class="bg-colour--primary-surface bg-mask bg-mask--t-convex ai-open-bg ai-scope" style="display: none;"></div><section class="home-green-investing position-relative p-y-spacer-xs ai-open-bg ai-scope" style="display: none;"><div class="container"><div class="row"><div class="col-12"><div class="flex-center"><h2 class="text-center m-b-spacer-sm" data-content="1-143735">Invest in Southwark Green Investment today</h2></div><div class="flex-center"><div class="ai-custom ai-open-investments"><div id="ai-open-councils"></div></div></div></div></div></div></section><div class="bg-colour--primary-surface bg-mask bg-mask--b-convex ai-open-bg ai-scope" style="display: none;"></div><section class="home-financial m-y-spacer-md p-y-spacer-xl mx-auto choke-800 ai-scope"><div class="container"><div class="row"><div class="col-12"><div class="flex-center"><h2 class="text-center" data-content="1-143736">How your money is being used</h2></div><div class="flex-center"><p class="body--lg text-center choke-800 m-b-spacer-lg"><span data-content="2-143745">Southwark Green Investment has already funded projects that&nbsp;save residents money, clean its air and protect residents from overheating and flooding. These include acceleration of its successful LED lighting programme, which has now replaced all 17,000 streetlights in the borough – saving the council energy and money. It also helped fund major investment in energy efficiency at leisure centres, with a new building management system and solar panels for Peckham Pulse leisure centre, and Crampton Primary School in Walworth has had energy efficiency upgrades.&nbsp;<br><br>Your investment has also funded&nbsp;community-led biodiversity projects across the borough, particularly in unused grey spaces on housing estates, including a scheme in the Kirby Estate to de-pave an old bin storage area to create the new&nbsp;<a href="https://www.instagram.com/reel/DQjOSR9jNLJ/" target="" rel="">Moreton Gate Nature Garden</a>.&nbsp;It has&nbsp;also&nbsp;supported the green economy by&nbsp;investing in an expansion of&nbsp;<a href="https://participate.libraryofthings.co.uk/southwark" target="" rel="">Library of Things</a>&nbsp;with two new sites in the borough – in East Dulwich and Elephant and Castle, and funded installation of 21 new cycle hangars to encourage active, low carbon travel.</span></p></div><div class="flex-center ai-uof-wrap"><div id="ai-use-of-funds"><div id="council-bar-chart"><div class="cbc-card"><section class="cbc-summary" id="cbc-summary" aria-live="polite"><div class="cbc-summary-inner"><div class="cbc-summary-logo"><a class="cbc-summary-logo-link" href="https://www.abundanceinvestment.com/council/southwark" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><div class="cbc-logo-badge" style="background:#00873b;"><img src="https://cdn4.sharein.com/abundance/cms/4f1c1b99-9a98-44bc-b9bc-4feea9064138.png" alt="Southwark Council logo"></div></a></div><div class="cbc-summary-lines" role="list"><div class="cbc-summary-line" role="listitem">4 investments</div><div class="cbc-summary-line" role="listitem">£1.68m spent</div><div class="cbc-summary-line" role="listitem">14 projects financed</div></div></div></section><div class="cbc-chart" id="cbc-chart"><div class="cbc-row"><div class="cbc-label">Energy efficiency</div><div class="cbc-bar-wrapper"><div class="cbc-bar-fill" data-final-width="53.3543751265142" style="width: 53.3544%; background: rgb(55, 235, 255);"><span class="cbc-bar-value">53.4%</span></div></div></div><div class="cbc-row"><div class="cbc-label">Renewable energy</div><div class="cbc-bar-wrapper"><div class="cbc-bar-fill" data-final-width="15.333717612672231" style="width: 15.3337%; background: rgb(247, 215, 231);"><span class="cbc-bar-value">15.3%</span></div></div></div><div class="cbc-row"><div class="cbc-label">Clean transportation</div><div class="cbc-bar-wrapper"><div class="cbc-bar-fill" data-final-width="14.767020295384867" style="width: 14.767%; background: rgb(241, 202, 141);"><span class="cbc-bar-value">14.8%</span></div></div></div><div class="cbc-row"><div class="cbc-label">Living and natural resources</div><div class="cbc-bar-wrapper"><div class="cbc-bar-fill" data-final-width="11.79861022349878" style="width: 11.7986%; background: rgb(33, 224, 244);"><span class="cbc-bar-value">11.8%</span></div></div></div><div class="cbc-row"><div class="cbc-label">Pollution prevention and control</div><div class="cbc-bar-wrapper"><div class="cbc-bar-fill" data-final-width="4.746276741929933" style="width: 4.74628%; background: rgb(250, 190, 128);"><span class="cbc-bar-value">4.7%</span></div></div></div></div><section class="cbc-projects"><h3 class="cbc-projects__title">Top projects financed</h3><div class="cbc-projects__list"><details class="cbc-proj"><summary class="cbc-proj__sum"><div class="cbc-proj__pill" style="background:#37ebff;color:#111827;border:1px solid rgba(17,24,39,.10);">Energy Efficiency</div><div class="cbc-proj__titleRow"><h4 class="cbc-proj__name">LED street lighting upgrades on highways</h4><div class="cbc-proj__right"><span class="cbc-proj__spent">£290,000.00</span><svg class="cbc-proj__chev" viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path fill="currentColor" d="M5.3 7.3a1 1 0 0 1 1.4 0L10 10.6l3.3-3.3a1 1 0 1 1 1.4 1.4l-4 4a1 1 0 0 1-1.4 0l-4-4a1 1 0 0 1 0-1.4z"></path></svg></div></div></summary><div class="cbc-proj__body"><p>Transitioning street lighting on highways to low-carbon, energy-efficient LEDs wich use 75% less energy than traditional lighting, helping to cut energy consumption, emissions and costs. </p><p>In addition, LEDs last much longer before needing to be replaced, even up to as much as 50,000 hours more. That means the council have to replace them less, helping to reduce waste and save money. LEDs are also free of toxic chemicals like mercury which is found in previous fluorescent lighting, making them safer and easier to recycle.</p></div></details><details class="cbc-proj"><summary class="cbc-proj__sum"><div class="cbc-proj__pill" style="background:#37ebff;color:#111827;border:1px solid rgba(17,24,39,.10);">Energy Efficiency</div><div class="cbc-proj__titleRow"><h4 class="cbc-proj__name">Leisure centres decarbonisation</h4><div class="cbc-proj__right"><span class="cbc-proj__spent">£250,000.00</span><svg class="cbc-proj__chev" viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path fill="currentColor" d="M5.3 7.3a1 1 0 0 1 1.4 0L10 10.6l3.3-3.3a1 1 0 1 1 1.4 1.4l-4 4a1 1 0 0 1-1.4 0l-4-4a1 1 0 0 1 0-1.4z"></path></svg></div></div></summary><div class="cbc-proj__body"><p>Installing new building management systems (BEMS) which use data, smart technologies and other energy efficiency solutions to identify inefficiencies, regulate and save energy.</p><p>This new system is expected to reduce our energy consumption at leisure centres by 10%, saving the council  £125,000 and cutting carbon emissions by 71 tonnes every year.</p><p>Furthermore, roof mounted solar panels have been installed on Peckham Pulse Leisure Centre - funded in conjunction with a grant from Sports England. This will further cut carbon emissions and reliance of fossil fuels</p></div></details><details class="cbc-proj"><summary class="cbc-proj__sum"><div class="cbc-proj__pill" style="background:#37ebff;color:#111827;border:1px solid rgba(17,24,39,.10);">Energy Efficiency</div><div class="cbc-proj__titleRow"><h4 class="cbc-proj__name">LED street lighting upgrades in parks</h4><div class="cbc-proj__right"><span class="cbc-proj__spent">£190,000.00</span><svg class="cbc-proj__chev" viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path fill="currentColor" d="M5.3 7.3a1 1 0 0 1 1.4 0L10 10.6l3.3-3.3a1 1 0 1 1 1.4 1.4l-4 4a1 1 0 0 1-1.4 0l-4-4a1 1 0 0 1 0-1.4z"></path></svg></div></div></summary><div class="cbc-proj__body"><p>Transitioning current lighting in Southwark's parks to low-carbon, energy-efficient LEDs. LEDs wich use 75% less energy than traditional lighting, helping to cut energy consumption, emissions and costs. </p><p>In addition, LEDs last much longer before needing to be replaced, even up to as much as 50,000 hours more. That means the council have to replace them less, helping to reduce waste and save money. LEDs are also free of toxic chemicals like mercury which is found in previous fluorescent lighting, making them safer and easier to recycle.</p></div></details></div></section></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></section